{"id": "EUVD-2026-101395", "enisaUuid": "ea46b991-907b-3d88-9f7a-4d6d7adffd01", "description": "An Out-of-bounds Write vulnerability in the routing protocol daemon (rpd) of Juniper Networks Junos OS and Junos OS Evolved allows an attacker with access to a configured BGP EVPN peer to cause a denial of service via BGP EVPN route processing when the l2vpn-evpn RIB telemetry sensor is subscribed. Successful exploitation can crash rpd and interrupt routing protocols until the daemon restarts and reconverges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T16:57:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T20:26:08", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:L/AU:Y/R:A/V:C/RE:M", "references": ["https://supportportal.juniper.net/JSA112187"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102179", "GHSA-3rhf-56vm-wgqj"], "assigner": "juniper", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b583c8a-ea93-3324-b2d8-b2df982b079d", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "23.4 <23.4R2-S8.13"}, {"id": "122afb28-d601-319d-80c9-17b0a58a77b7", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "26.2 <26.2R1-S2-EVO"}, {"id": "17498b79-622d-374b-b1ed-5197c13467e0", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "25.4 <25.4R1-S3-EVO"}, {"id": "1e579184-6ace-3445-aa25-442175aafb81", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "0 <23.2R2-S7.7-EVO"}, {"id": "43f33c27-560a-33d5-8606-a82d44dc8bac", "product": {"name": "Junos OS Evolved", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "25.4X300 <25.4X300-D40-EVO"}, {"id": "53460b3e-728c-362e-8702-d967446eebd3", "product": {"name": "Junos OS", "vendor": {"name": "Juniper Networks"}}, "product_version": "0 <23.2R2-S7.7"}, {"id": "654547d9-0244-37e4-beb0-54fbe5fd7800", "product": {"name": "Junos OS",